      "rev_n_4_9dfb6f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_9dfb6f_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_9dfb6f",
        "thought_text": "Revisit the grouping logic. Ensure that names are grouped correctly based on their starting sequences, and that the groups are formed such that any name with a common prefix appears within the same group.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "7174090622780025954",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408067.904448
      },
      "rev_n_5_c52d8e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_c52d8e_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_c52d8e",
        "thought_text": "Consider using dynamic programming to count the number of valid permutations. Define a state that tracks the current prefix and the count of names that start with that prefix, then transition between states based on adding new names with compatible prefixes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "7174090622780025954",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408067.904475
      },
      "rev_n_6_f6346c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_f6346c_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_f6346c",
        "thought_text": "Implement a recursive approach with memoization to explore all possible valid orderings. The recursion should attempt to place names in positions while respecting the prefix constraints, and memoize results to avoid redundant calculations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "7174090622780025954",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408067.904486
      },
      "rev_n_7_62f891_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_62f891_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_62f891",
        "thought_text": "The current approach groups names by their prefixes, but it doesn't account for the constraints properly. We need to ensure that names with the same prefix are treated as a single block, and the blocks themselves can be permuted.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4982432419961948924",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408094.7489128
      },
      "rev_n_8_3bfb3e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_3bfb3e_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_3bfb3e",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a tree structure where each node represents a prefix, and its children represent further prefixes. The number of valid orderings would then be the product of factorials of the sizes of each subtree plus one (for the root node).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4982432419961948924",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408094.748936
      },
      "rev_n_9_edfd24_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_edfd24_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_edfd24",
        "thought_text": "Implement a recursive function to calculate the number of valid orderings. For each prefix, calculate the number of ways to order the names starting with that prefix and multiply by the number of ways to order the remaining names.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4982432419961948924",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408094.748947
      },
      "rev_n_10_8d3b8d_0": {
